        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "9e7f2df6-3e03-512e-931c-e7924c18ae15",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Rudolf Schwarzkogler, Howard Zieff, Günter Brus, Otto Mühl, Hermann Nitsch, Yocheved Weinfeld\n- Organizations: Debel Gallery, Viennese Actionism\n- Places: Vienna\n- Roles: performance artist, director, television commercial director, advertising photographer\n- Events: Debel Gallery exhibitions, performance of \"Nidah\"\n\nFacts:\n- Rudolf Schwarzkogler was born on 13 November 1940 in Vienna and died on 20 June 1969 in Vienna.\n- Rudolf Schwarzkogler was an Austrian performance artist closely associated with the Viennese Actionism group.\n- The Viennese Actionism group included Günter Brus, Otto Mühl, and Hermann Nitsch.\n- Howard B. Zieff was born on 21 October 1927 and died on 22 February 2009.\n- Howard B. Zieff was an American director, television commercial director, and advertising photographer.\n- Debel Gallery exhibited avant-garde artists, which was unusual for a private gallery.\n- In 1974, Debel Gallery exhibited the Austrian artist Rudolf Schwarzkogler.\n- In 1976, Debel Gallery staged a performance of \"Nidah\" by Yocheved Weinfeld.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "813f93d5-61d4-5f7d-912c-9c709c02584c",
        "text": "Page: Rudolf Schwarzkogler. Sentence: Rudolf Schwarzkogler (13 November 1940, Vienna – 20 June 1969, Vienna) was an Austrian performance artist closely associated with the Viennese Actionism group that included artists Günter Brus, Otto Mühl, and Hermann Nitsch.\nPage: Howard Zieff. Sentence: Howard B. Zieff (21 October 1927 – 22 February 2009), (pronounced Zeef ) was an American director, television commercial director, and advertising photographer.\nPage: Debel Gallery. Sentence: In addition, the Gallery exhibited avant-garde artists, which was unusual for a private gallery; for example, in 1974 the Austrian artist Rudolf Schwarzkogler, and in 1976 the Gallery staged a performance of \"Nidah\" by Yocheved Weinfeld.",
